&lt;p&gt;Please note this role requires you to be in the office 5 days a week.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;At Culture Amp, our People Experience team exists to create a better world of work — starting with our own Campers. As our Workplace Experience Partner for EMEA, you&#39;ll be the heartbeat of our London and Berlin offices: the person who keeps things running smoothly, makes Campers feel genuinely welcomed and connected, and brings our office culture to life every single day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, people-first role that blends operational rigour with creative energy. You&#39;ll own the day-to-day running of our two EMEA offices, design and deliver events that foster real connection and belonging, and act as the go-to point of contact for 100 Campers and leaders across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because your global team is based across different time zones, you&#39;ll bring a strong sense of self-direction and ownership to everything you do — proactively solving problems, managing competing priorities, and making the EMEA office experience something Campers are proud of.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As part of this team of amazing humans, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage the day-to-day&lt;/strong&gt; — Own the inner workings of the offices within the region, being present in the London office 5 days a week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own EMEA office operations&lt;/strong&gt; — Manage the day-to-day running of our London and Berlin offices, ensuring a compliant, safe, and appealing workplace. This includes overseeing office works, repairs, maintenance, and vendor relationships, and staying current with local health, safety, and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and deliver meaningful events&lt;/strong&gt; — Build and execute a regular cadence of impactful in-person and remote-friendly events and coordinated moments that foster Camper connection and belonging across the EMEA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the on-the-ground partner for EMEA&lt;/strong&gt; — Proactively engage with local leaders and Campers, acting as the primary point of contact and advocate for office plans, initiatives, and the overall regional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Campers day-to-day&lt;/strong&gt; — Serve as the first point of contact for Camper inquiries and manage request tickets within the dedicated SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage the regional budget&lt;/strong&gt; — Own spend against the allocated EMEA budget, including timely and accurate processing of invoices and expenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilities and vendor management experience&lt;/strong&gt; — A proven ability to manage office operations, repairs and maintenance, and vendor relationships in a fast-paced, in-person environment. In addition to liaising with landlords and building management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event planning and execution skills&lt;/strong&gt; — A track record of designing and running engaging workplace events and connection moments for a distributed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong stakeholder communication&lt;/strong&gt; — You&#39;re a confident, clear communicator who builds trust quickly with local leaders, Campers, and cross-functional teams (including PX, Internal Comms, and IT/Facilities).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability and problem-solving ability&lt;/strong&gt; — You thrive when juggling competing day-to-day priorities and resolve office and Camper issues proactively and calmly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-motivation and independence&lt;/strong&gt; — Working with a global team, you&#39;re able to self-motivate, prioritise, and drive work independently and with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
